## Nextjs Frontend

- Container component and presentational component should be in different files.

```tsx
// components/Counter/CounterPresentation.jsx
// Presentation component - only handles rendering

export default function CounterPresentation({ count, onIncrement, onDecrement }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Count: {count}</h2>
      <button onClick={onIncrement}>+</button>
      <button onClick={onDecrement}>-</button>
    </div>
  );
}

// components/Counter/CounterContainer.jsx
// Container component - handles state and logic

import { useState } from 'react';
import CounterPresentation from './CounterPresentation';

export default function CounterContainer() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  const increment = () => setCount(count + 1);
  const decrement = () => setCount(count - 1);

  return (
    <CounterPresentation 
      count={count}
      onIncrement={increment}
      onDecrement={decrement}
    />
  );
}

// pages/index.js
// Usage in a Next.js page

import CounterContainer from '../components/Counter/CounterContainer';

export default function HomePage() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Counter Example</h1>
      <CounterContainer />
    </div>
  );
}
```

- Keep each component as small as possible.
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication.
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes.
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
- Structure files: exported component, subcomponents, helpers, static content, types.
- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/auth-wizard).
- Favor named exports for components.

```ts
export const Button = ({ name, age }: ButtonProps) => {
  return <button>{name}</button>;
};
```

- Use TypeScript for all code; prefer interfaces over types.
- Use enums instead of maps.
- Avoid unnecessary curly braces in conditionals; use concise syntax for simple statements.
- Use declarative TSX.
- Use the "function" keyword for pure functions.
- Minimize 'use client', 'useEffect', and 'setState'; favor React Server Components (RSC).
- Wrap client components in Suspense with fallback.
- Use dynamic loading for non-critical components.
- Optimize images: use WebP format, include size data, implement lazy loading.
- Use Shadcn UI, Radix UI and Tailwind for components and styling.
- Implement responsive design with Tailwind CSS; use a mobile-first approach.
- New component have a Props type as separate type

```ts
type ButtonProps = {
  name: string;
  age: number;
};

// Example of a component
const Button = ({ name, age }: ButtonProps) => {
  return <button>{name}</button>;
};
```

- Graphql using apollo client: use useQuery and useMutation and have to add type for them (useMutation<T, Variables>)
- Graphql api folder should have both document and script. Document file should define all the fields that can be used. Script file can define some of the fields that the UI need to show.

```ts
// api/documents/bank/transaction.gql
query GetBankTransactions {
    getBankTransactions {
        id
        amount
        spentAmount
        createdAt
        description
        bank {
            name
        }
    }
}

// api/script/bank/transaction.ts
import { gql } from '@apollo/client';

export const GET_BANK_TRANSACTIONS = gql`
  query GetBankTransactions {
    getBankTransactions {
        id
        description
        bank {
            name
        }
    }
}
```

- React hook form: have a separate default value variable, a schema should put on a separate file in lib/schema folder
- Optimize Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, FID).
- Favor server components and Next.js SSR.
- Use only for Web API access in small components.
- Avoid for data fetching or state management.

## Nestjs Backend

- Each query or mutation should have a separate name instead of depending on the name of function

```ts
@Query(() => String, { name: 'getHello' })
async hello(): Promise<string> {
  return 'Hello, world!';
}
```

- Args pass through query or mutation have to be defined in dto file put in same level dtos folder. Args should have a data field which is defined by input type

```ts
@InputType()
export class HelloDto {
  @Field(() => String)
  data: string;
}

@ArgsType()
export class HelloArgs {
  @Field(() => HelloDto)
  @Type(() => HelloDto)
  @ValidateNested()
  data: HelloDto;
}
```

- Utilize auth user to get user id instead require it in args

```ts
@Query(() => String, { name: 'getHello' })
async hello(@AuthUser() user: User): Promise<string> {
  return this.helloService.hello(user.id);
}
```
